      "name": null,
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14252321/assets/e2ba81c227223d872727ceec1e6b097b69d3f4b47cd9f7190ab984c2124c1bf5.png)\n\nFor the triangle above, find $m∠A$ in degrees rounded to two decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "We use the Law of Cosines to solve for angle $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡A=\\frac{{b}^{2}+{c}^{2}-{a}^{2}}{2bc}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\na=5,\\,b=6,\\,c=7.\n$$\n\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡A & =\\frac{{6}^{2}+{7}^{2}-{5}^{2}}{2(6)(7)} \\\\  & =\\frac{36+49-25}{84} \\\\  & =\\frac{60}{84} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠A & =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{5}{7}) \\\\  & ={44.42}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places.",
